write down what the Noise board became, and tick what landed

The pipeline doc gained the complement: the three cases a sibling lane can be in
and why a failure is not the third of them, the tail the lane now adds, the empty
complement the host settles without a seat, and the fact that the grouping is the
only thing the seat can get wrong.

The sidecar doc gained the disclosure clause it was owed. The health report names
the daemon's board server as local, once a lane is actually open and not before —
a status field claiming a running loopback server while none runs is a lie in the
UI, which is why group 2 left the clause unmet rather than writing it early.
